{"body":"## Summary

The crowdsec module writes generated files (e.g. `/etc/crowdsec/profiles.yaml`) via `systemd.tmpfiles` `f+` rules, but puts the generated content into the `argument` field without escaping `%`. `systemd-tmpfiles` expands specifiers in `argument`, so a `%` coming from user config is treated as a specifier. `%d` is not a valid tmpfiles specifier, so the rule is rejected and the file is never written.

The failure is silent: `systemd-tmpfiles` exits with 65 (`DATAERR`), which is listed in `SuccessExitStatus` of the NixOS tmpfiles service, so `nixos-rebuild switch` does not report an error.

## Reproduction

```nix
services.crowdsec = {
  enable = true;
  settings.profiles = [{
    name = "test";
    filters = [ "Alert.Remediation == true" ];
    decisions = [{
      type = "ban";
      duration_expr = "Sprintf('%dh', 4)";
    }];
  }];
};
```

After `nixos-rebuild switch`:

```
systemd-tmpfiles[...]: Failed to substitute specifiers in argument: Invalid slot
```

and `/etc/crowdsec/profiles.yaml` does not exist.

`Sprintf('%dh', ...)` is the documented way to use `duration_expr`, so this is not an exotic configuration.

## Cause

In `nixos/modules/services/security/crowdsec/default.nix`:

```nix
createFile = dstPath: content: {
  name = dstPath;
  value."f+" = {
    user = cfg.user;
    group = cfg.group;
    argument = content;   # not escaped
  };
};
```

`tmpfiles.d(5)` states: "Specifiers can be used in the "path" and "argument" fields. An unknown or unresolvable specifier is treated as invalid configuration."

## Suggested fix

Escape `%` in the payload:

```nix
argument = lib.replaceStrings [ "%" ] [ "%%" ] content;
```

This should ideally apply to all `f+` entries (profiles, console, acquisitions, simulation), or those files could be generated in the store and referenced via `L+`/`C+` instead.

## Environment

- nixpkgs: `02c087f3fe673c9e317f206a627cb6b910336dbe` (nixos-unstable)
- systemd: 262
"}

