{"body":"### Nixpkgs version

- Unstable (26.11)

### Describe the bug

share/1password/chrome_crashpad_handler isn't given libglib-2.0.so.0. 8.12.40, the current package, tolerates it. 8.12.42 aborts at startup with SIGTRAP and nothing in its log. Most likely the newer Electron refuses to run without a working crashpad handler. The next version bump will probably hit this.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Override _1password-gui (nixos-unstable) to 8.12.42 (src = https://downloads.1password.com/linux/tar/stable/x86_64/1password-8.12.42.x64.tar.gz).
2. Run 1password:
…/share/1password/chrome_crashpad_handler: error while loading shared libraries: libglib-2.0.so.0: cannot open shared object file
   The process dumps core with SIGTRAP; it's the same on Wayland and X11, with or without --no-sandbox and --disable-gpu.

### Minimal reproducer

```nix

{
  inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/02c087f3fe673c9e317f206a627cb6b910336dbe";

  outputs =
    { nixpkgs, ... }:
    let
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      pkgs = import nixpkgs { inherit system; config.allowUnfree = true; };
    in
    {
      packages.${system} = {
        # stock 8.12.40: crashpad handler already lacks libglib (tolerated)
        stock = pkgs._1password-gui;
        # 8.12.42: same packaging, aborts at startup with SIGTRAP
        default = pkgs._1password-gui.overrideAttrs (_: rec {
          version = "8.12.42";
          src = pkgs.fetchurl {
            url = "https://downloads.1password.com/linux/tar/stable/x86_64/1password-${version}.x64.tar.gz";
            sha256 = "1phqhim7r6ywlgnfms5lbkrsy0dy22fhg6kk112gvmixsldlvric";
          };
        });
      };
    };
}

```

### Expected behaviour

1password GUI and CLI can be launched and work

### Screenshots

( I needed the latest version 8-12-42)

$ ldd …/1password-8.12.40/share/1password/chrome_crashpad_handler | grep glib
        libglib-2.0.so.0 => not found
$ ldd …/1password-8.12.42/share/1password/chrome_crashpad_handler | grep glib
        libglib-2.0.so.0 => not found

### Relevant log output

```console

```

### Additional context

Add glib to the wrapper's library path (or add glib to the existing LD_LIBRARY_PATH / runtimeDependencies):
nativeBuildInputs = old.nativeBuildInputs ++ [ makeWrapper ];
postFixup = (old.postFixup or "") + ''
  wrapProgram $out/bin/1password --prefix LD_LIBRARY_PATH : ${glib.out}/lib
'';
With that, 8.12.42 starts, the vault opens and the SSH agent works.

### System metadata

NixOS 26.05 (26.05.12297.cd4ea8d57de1), kernel 6.18.57, Hyprland 0.55.4 (Wayland), NVIDIA 595.71.05. Package taken from nixos-unstable, overridden to 8.12.42.

